1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:01,637
Jotaro!

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:04,191
Do you hear what you're saying right now?!

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:07,560
Of course I do.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,005
Finally starting to lose
your hearing, old man.

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:14,032
Obviously, I just told him my next pitch.

6
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:17,520
I'm gonna win with a
high outside fastball.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,437
But, Jotaro, you...

8
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,440
Will you believe me?

9
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,720
Or will you doubt me instead?

10
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:27,710
Hmph.

11
00:00:27,793 --> 00:00:28,932
Not too bright, are you?

12
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,717
My stand peers into
your soul the same way a

13
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,447
thermal imager detects
an object's radiation.

14
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,420
Say what you will, your soul cannot lie.

15
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:46,231
Regardless of what it is,

16
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:50,478
by analyzing your soul I can see the
answer to any yes or no question.

17
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:54,440
Right or left, high or
low, outside or inside,

18
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:58,860
fastball or curveball, my
stand's perception is infallible.

19
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,914
this is characters now on your channel.

20
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:37,000
We're still looking at the
destination of the enemy.

21
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:43,540
We're still looking at the end
of the battle of the battle.

22
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:54,357
The battle of the battle
is the end of the battle.

23
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:55,397
Thank

24
00:01:55,480 --> 00:02:02,480
you

25
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,130
so

26
00:02:13,213 --> 00:02:14,043
much

27
00:02:14,126 --> 00:02:19,420
for

28
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:23,910
watching.

29
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:34,620
Will your pitch be a
high outside fastball?

30
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:37,200
Yes or no?

31
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,748
Well, Chotaro's telling
the truth after all.

32
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:46,980
He's really going to pitch
a high outside fastball.

33
00:02:47,380 --> 00:02:48,480
What's he up to?

34
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,097
It's true that he beat
my brother by bluffing,

35
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:55,239
But he's a fool if he thinks the
same tired tactic will work with me.

36
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,560
Here it comes.

37
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:02,920
For your sake,

38
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:07,884
I hope you haven't forgotten that you'll
lose the game if you fall 11 runs behind.

39
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,397
Was that...

40
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,420
a curve? Impossible!

41
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,780
I thought he was going for
a high outside fastball!

42
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:21,100
He hits, but it's a grounder!

43
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,480
The ball is thrown to first and out!

44
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,460
There's just no way!

45
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:37,537
Everything about him said he was going
to throw a high outside fastball!

46
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:39,060
His soul can't lie!

47
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,300
No one's can!

48
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,660
Not a Zen master!

49
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:42,977
Not even my brother!

50
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,917
And he's the world's greatest con man!

51
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,060
Next up is another high-outside fastball.

52
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,400
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

53
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:53,340
What the hell?

54
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,993
He's telling the truth!

55
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:58,997
Jotaro, you have the goal to
cheat your way to victory?

56
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,500
He actually is cheating!

57
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,060
A low inside forkball!

58
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,037
It's a fly ball heading for the pitcher!

59
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,950
Out!

60
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,840
You must have cheated! Admit it!

61
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,840
You bastard!

62
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,857
You clearly tampered with the console!

63
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,713
He's telling the truth?

64
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,677
I know you're cheating me!

65
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:32,642
You have to be!

66
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,840
Would you just come clean already?

67
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,540
No response! Yes! Damn it! That's right!

68
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,387
I only have use of my power if
I ask him a yes or no question!

69
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:50,528
Judging from your scared expression,
your power requires a yes or no question.

70
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,437
It's like your brother used to say.

71
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:57,167
This is just a dance of deception
where the loser cries first.

72
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,480
A dance, eh?

73
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,940
So this is nothing but a game to you?

74
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,580
How dare you!

75
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:06,357
Are you taking me for a fool?

76
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,457
Have you any idea who you're speaking to?

77
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,720
Jotaro pitch the ball.

78
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:14,905
I'll figure out your little trick
and take your soul as my prize

79
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,080
All right

80
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,300
Let's continue for my next pitch.

81
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,780
I'll throw a high outside fastball

82
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,900
Yes, yes, yes, yes

83
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:31,437
Once again, his soul says
he's telling the truth.

84
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:34,461
He's really going to pitch
a high outside fastball

85
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:37,577
I've had about as much
of this as I can take.

86
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,740
This ends now.

87
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:42,805
I'll figure out how you're cheating
if it's the last thing I do!

88
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,340
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

89
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,897
So, Chiyotaro hasn't changed his mind.

90
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:53,039
He's still dead set on
throwing that infernal pitch.

91
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,150
It's coming.

92
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:55,860
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

93
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:59,552
So far, it's still a fastball,
and his soul is saying yes.

94
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,700
It changed direction!

95
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,180
A forkball!

96
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,550
What?

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,588
It's a different pitch now!

98
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:07,720
Yes, yes, yes.

99
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,310
Out!

100
00:06:10,393 --> 00:06:12,000
That's three outs! Change!

101
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:13,650
Oh.

102
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,560
I don't get it.

103
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:20,232
Why can't I figure out how he's cheating?

104
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:23,197
Jotaro's soul kept saying
he'd throw a fastball,

105
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:26,162
but at the last second it
curved into a forkball.

106
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,980
This doesn't make any sense!

107
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,490
How?

108
00:06:30,573 --> 00:06:32,800
How is this wretch deceiving me?

109
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,940
You're gonna lose this game, Darby.

110
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,360
Shut your mouth!

111
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,700
Come on, tell me why you
removed your stupid hat!

112
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,957
I'm more perceptive than you think.

113
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,457
I know you've been cheating
ever since you took it off.

114
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,716
Now move, I want to check
your station and controller.

115
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,575
There's nothing here.

116
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,750
Damn you!

117
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:01,180
How did you do it?

118
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:04,357
It must have something to
do with that hat of yours.

119
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,337
Isn't that right?

120
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:06,920
No, no, no, no.

121
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:12,057
There must be evidence
around here somewhere.

122
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,597
You're using Star Platinum
to cheat, aren't you?

123
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,320
No, no, no, no.

124
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,880
Just admit it.

125
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,317
You're doing something.

126
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,320
Damn it. Damn it.

127
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,537
I can clearly read Jotaro's thoughts,

128
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:31,517
which means my stand's power
is still working as it should.

129
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:35,020
So how can his mind say one
thing but his body do another?

130
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:37,300
Hey, Jotaro, are you seeing this?

131
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,597
Looks like he's losing his youthful glow.

132
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:43,033
He definitely doesn't look
like a guy in his 20s anymore.

133
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:46,097
Darby, it's your turn to pitch, so hurry.

134
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,474
We don't have all day.

135
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:48,810
It's four to three.

136
00:07:48,893 --> 00:07:51,797
With only a one point difference,
I might still have a chance.

137
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,580
I am a video game genius.

138
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,800
I can't lose.

139
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:56,740
I am a video game genius.

140
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:57,897
I can't lose!

141
00:07:57,980 --> 00:08:00,156
I've won every game I've ever played!

142
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,182
I'm invincible!

143
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,037
A video game expert is an expert at life!

144
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:07,120
Do you think you can shake
my confidence so easily?

145
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,620
Look at that!

146
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,760
Another home run!

147
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:15,317
That's another run for the Jaguars, folks!

148
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,560
It's five to three!

149
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:29,060
It can't be!

150
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:33,000
I accidentally released his
soul from the doll! Look!

151
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,137
His soul has returned to his body!

152
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,926
He's regaining consciousness!

153
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,700
No! I didn't!

154
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,506
I never once admitted defeat!

155
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,758
It was an accident!

156
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,477
I didn't mean to release
his soul from the doll!

157
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,089
But the thing is, you
did release his soul.

158
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,971
You know what that means.

159
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:54,560
Your soul admitted defeat
and it's game over.

160
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,317
Huh? Hold on. Is...

161
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,740
is Joseph's stand?

162
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:05,360
It was wrapped around the controller
the entire time! Huh? Whoops.

163
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,580
I guess I forgot to put this away.

164
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,600
How could something so stupid... No.

165
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,177
You mean it was Joseph?

166
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,837
He was the cheater all along?

167
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:14,780
Damn it!

168
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:16,717
Jotaro is telling the truth.

169
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,682
He really wasn't controlling it.

170
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,860
It was you, Joseph Joestar! Hmm?

171
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,420
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

172
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,233
That's right, good boy.

173
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:28,657
Too bad you're not your brother.

174
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:32,681
Because if you were, you would have
figured it out a long time ago.

175
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:39,620
By the way, old man, you're pretty clever.

176
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:42,697
I didn't expect you to catch on
to my idea as quickly as you did.

177
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,417
Well, of course I did, my boy.

178
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,088
I can read you like a book.

179
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,080
You are my grandson, after all.

180
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,960
Now, up and at him, Kakyoin.

181
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:53,810
Damn.

182
00:09:53,893 --> 00:09:55,677
Joseph was controlling things from behind.

183
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,840
Before I forget.

184
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:01,560
What to do with you, you
button-mashing jerk? Oh, shit.

185
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,351
Please, mercy, I beg you.

186
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,017
I've already given you back
Kakyoin's soul, haven't I?

187
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:09,060
It's like they say, no
harm, no foul. We're good.

188
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:10,557
Right, right, right.

189
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:12,977
You wanna know whether I'll forgive you?

190
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:16,354
Why don't you just do what
you do best and read my mind?

191
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:19,560
No, no, no, no, no!

192
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:22,440
Answer this.

193
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:26,057
Will I hit you with my right fist
or decide to deck you with my left?

194
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:27,140
I'd love to know.

195
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:30,698
Well, since you're asking,
you'll use your right one?

196
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:33,180
No, no, no, no, no!

197
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,240
Then your left?

198
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:38,080
No, no, no, no, no!

199
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,915
You're not going to use both, are you?

200
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:43,480
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

201
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,250
Yes.

202
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,616
Are you going to do the Aurora thing?

203
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,340
Yes, yes, yes.

204
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:51,220
Oh, my god.

205
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,780
Darby Younger, out of commission.

206
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,580
How about that?

207
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,197
We broke through some sort of wall.

208
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,045
That's our ticket out of here!

209
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:10,940
Jotaro, cock you in!

210
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:12,700
Good grief.

211
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:27,640
Forgive me for disturbing you, but Your
Excellence, as I'm sure you're aware,

212
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:31,514
Jostar and his comrades have
just infiltrated the manor.

213
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:35,920
Regrettably, I must also inform
you that Darby has been defeated.

214
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:43,080
Oh, but Darby was a genius.

215
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:46,380
How could one as gifted as Darby fail me?

216
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,900
Come, I'd like to hear your thoughts.

217
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:52,380
You may enter Cool Ice.

218
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,380
As you wish.

219
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:15,240
Always remember this,
whatever the obstacle,

220
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:16,877
whatever the danger,

221
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:21,740
the Joestars are prepared to sacrifice
their lives in order to save their family.

222
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:25,940
Kakyoin and the other two,
what were their names again?

223
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:30,500
Ah yes, I believe it's
Avdol and Polnareff.

224
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:35,211
They're willing to surrender their lives
for the eradication of yours truly.

225
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:41,040
They believe fleeing from me is somehow
the same as running from themselves.

226
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,940
Fools, one and all.

227
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:49,040
Nonetheless, the fools find
strength in this misguided belief.

228
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:52,120
Darby swore his undying loyalty.

229
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:57,060
But unfortunately, he was not
prepared to actually die on my behalf.

230
00:12:57,820 --> 00:13:02,400
Which is why, at the edge of glory,
victory slipped through his fingers.

231
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:07,540
For the rest of eternity,
Darby will remain in ignorance.

232
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,600
Ice, have a look at the scar on my neck.

233
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:17,900
Jonathan Joestar's body
is still rejecting me,

234
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:22,357
but I need the blood of one more soul
before this body truly becomes mine.

235
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:24,969
And once that happens,
the wound will heal.

236
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:30,737
Ice, will you offer me the crimson
vigor coursing through your veins?

237
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:33,280
Yes, it'd be an honor.

238
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:48,660
What is mine is yours.

239
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,940
Ah, you beheaded yourself.

240
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:13,880
Most splendid.

241
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,260
What cool ice.

242
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,620
I cannot accept the blood
of such a loyal servant.

243
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:23,120
My wound shall be healed, but it
will be with the blood of another.

244
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,040
For now, you must live.

245
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,977
So awaken and be reborn.

246
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:34,940
Your steadfast resolve shall secure
your victory over those who'd oppose me.

247
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,940
I shall not fail you, my lord.

248
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:45,000
No weapon can surpass one's own body.

249
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,160
You are ready, Kulice.

250
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,460
Now go and attend to our unwanted guests.

251
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:56,700
I swear, Lord Dio, I
will not let you down.

252
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,540
You have my word.

253
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,440
I'll destroy them all.

254
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,800
Well, I sincerely hope that for your sake,

255
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:25,608
your next victim into the void will be
one of the Joestars and not my boudoir.

256
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,417
The ten minutes he gave us are up.

257
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:37,420
I know that Mr.

258
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,977
Joestar ordered us to
set the mansion on fire.

259
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:41,340
But I say we go.

260
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,660
We have to find them. Agreed.

